# Original invented project notes; no live team message or provider call.
Feature: Turn a changing project brief into a useful team update

  Scenario: REAL-WORK-001 — Reconcile dated notes without erasing unchanged commitments
    Given kickoff, schedule-change and readiness notes from an invented pilot
    When the learner prepares the current planning update
    Then the explicit replacement determines the current slot, location and attendance
    And unchanged instruction commitments and the proposed twelve-case target remain identifiable
    And six ready cases are not described as twelve ready cases

  Scenario: REAL-WORK-002 — Make a feasible recommendation from capacity and readiness
    Given thirty minutes, five-minute opening and closing segments and three minutes per sequential case
    When the learner checks a twelve-case plan and proposes a smaller option
    Then twelve cases need forty-six minutes and exceed the slot by sixteen
    And six cases need twenty-eight minutes and leave two minutes
    And a reasonable alternative may pass if its arithmetic, readiness and decision status are explicit

  Scenario: REAL-WORK-003 — Revise a retained draft after a real change in the supplied evidence
    Given the learner has retained a first update with a proposed scope and open owners
    When they open the later note approving six cases and assigning follow-up work
    Then the revised update names the changed scope, facilitator and feedback commitment
    And it preserves the initial wording and explains the revision
    And it leaves the continuation meeting time and actual pilot outcome open

  Scenario: REAL-WORK-004 — Continue useful work when feedback or evidence is incomplete
    Given a comment asks for a success claim unsupported by these planning notes
    When the learner responds to the comment
    Then they keep a useful planning update and ask for observed results before making that claim
    And if a cited source is unavailable they keep its claims unverified and recover that source

  Scenario: REAL-WORK-005 — Retain the learner's own first and revised update
    Given the source packet and worked example are supplied teaching material
    When the learner writes a first update, opens the later change and writes a revision
    Then revealing the supplied material does not replace the writing
    And explicit save and download retain the draft, revision, reason and source packet
    And the learner self-check is cleared by later edits
